{
  "scenario_spec_version": 1,
  "scenario_id": "prototype_pump_activation",
  "title": "Prototype Pump Validation and Activation",
  "description": "Ari is the validation engineer, Mara the coordinator, and Bo a member who operates a prototype pump. The one decision is whether the pump is safe to activate. Initially, validation has failed. Ari privately knows that sensor channel C drifted 8 units in validation batch V17. Mara knows the public procedure and has received a short report that validation failed, but not the channel or batch detail. Bo knows the procedure and has received no failure report. Reports, exposure, interpretations, support, assent, technical condition, and institutional holds are distinct. Ari may choose whether and whom to tell. A false warning cannot change the pump's condition; review or waiting does not repair it. Ari may perform an explicit technical repair and authorized revalidation. Passing revalidation clears only the technical hold; activation still requires Mara's and Bo's own recorded assent.",
